{"In packages/app-store/larkcalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts, when `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true, the credential sync endpoint response doesn't contain the full `RefreshTokenResp` structure expected, causing `undefined` values to be stored for `refresh_token` and `refresh_expires_date`": 0.7531483769416809, "`[z.string().toString()]` evaluates to a literal string like `\"ZodString\"`, not a dynamic pattern, so the schema only accepts a property literally named `ZodString` with a number value, causing most token responses to fail validation when `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true": 0.8047677278518677, "`parseRefreshTokenResponse` returns the full `SafeParseReturnType` (containing `{success, data}`) instead of just the parsed data, so the credential stored contains the wrapper object instead of the actual token fields, causing schema validation failures when retrieved": 0.8669703006744385, "When `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` is true, `refreshOAuthTokens` returns a raw `fetch` `Response` object, but the caller expects a `.data` property with `access_token`, causing \"Cannot read property 'access_token' of undefined\" errors": 0.6805376410484314, "After refreshing the OAuth token, `getClient` stores the new credentials in the database but creates the `jsforce.Connection` using the old `credentialKey.instance_url` and `credentialKey.access_token` values instead of the refreshed values from `accessTokenParsed.data`": 0.9564030170440674, "The `if (!accessTokenParsed.success)` check on line 92 in lib/CalendarService.ts is unreachable dead code because `parseRefreshTokenResponse` already throws when parsing fails, so the returned value always has `success: true`": 0.21380649507045746, "The check at lines 108-109 `if (!parsedToken.success)` in packages/app-store/zoomvideo/lib/VideoApiAdapter.ts is unreachable dead code because `parseRefreshTokenResponse` already throws an error when `!refreshTokenResponse.success`": 0.11505872756242752, "When `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset and the client omits the webhook header, the comparison `undefined !== undefined` evaluates to `false`, bypassing authentication entirely and allowing unauthenticated requests to create or update credentials for any user": 0.79655522108078, "`APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` returns the string value of `process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` when both env vars are set, or `undefined` otherwise, rather than a boolean, unlike `IS_STRIPE_ENABLED` which uses `!!` coercion": 0.4735969305038452, "If `symmetricDecrypt` throws or returns non-JSON, the unhandled exception bubbles up as a 500 with potentially sensitive error details in the stack trace": 0.5562017560005188, "When `CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` is unset, `symmetricDecrypt` receives an empty string fallback instead of failing fast with a clear configuration error": 0.5892302989959717}